{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778276955,"nonce":"2HMfjPLjYMijMy3L8NLrX/CY/ww=","title":"Compositional output-jerk loss term ‖x⃛ₜ‖² (mirrors StateDerivativeLoss)","message":"Adds `OutputJerkLoss` to `feedbax.loss` — a generic, compositional output-jerk penalty. Mirrors the just-merged `StateDerivativeLoss` (issue `e8f3738`, commit `380cbd1`), but operates on a state substate with cross-timestep order 2 instead of 1.\n\n## Surface\n\n- Class: `feedbax.loss.OutputJerkLoss(label, where, time_axis=1, norm)`\n- Default `where`: `lambda state: state.mechanics.effector.vel` — operating on velocity, the discrete second difference (`v_{t+1} - 2 v_t + v_{t-1}`) equals the discrete jerk (third derivative of position) up to a `dt` factor.\n- Default `norm`: squared L2 over feature axes.\n- Default `time_axis`: 1 (feedbax `(trial, time, ...)` rollout convention).\n- Returns a per-trial loss density via `mean(||v_{t+1} - 2 v_t + v_{t-1}||²)` along the time axis. `where` may return either a single `Array` or a `PyTree[Array]`; leaf contributions sum.\n\n## Order\n\n`order = 2` cross-timestep — needs `t-1, t, t+1`. Implemented via `jnp.diff(arr, n=2, axis=time_axis)`. Distinguishes from `StateDerivativeLoss` which has `order = 1`. This dovetails with feedbax `d67e303` (streaming-loss extension to support cross-timestep terms with declared order).\n\n## Properties to verify by tests\n- Zero on a constant-velocity (zero-jerk) trajectory.\n- Closed-form on a sinusoidal velocity profile (known second-difference magnitude).\n- Correct gradient sign (penalises larger temporal second-differences).\n- Wireable into `CompositeLoss`; weight=0 is a no-op (preserves existing configurations).\n- Invariant to a leading ensemble-vmap axis.\n\n## Motivation\n\nSurfaced from rlrmp issue `efc4d68` escalation order: jerk penalty on the output trajectory at weight 1e5 (Shahbazi, Codol, Michaels \u0026 Gribble 2025 Eq. 1). The first escalation (`StateDerivativeLoss`, `e8f3738`) has been merged onto develop; this is the parallel jerk term, ready to compose alongside it.\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- Smoothness term (parallel pattern): feedbax `e8f3738`.\n- rlrmp consumer: rlrmp `efc4d68` (baseline retrain + 2×2×2 architecture × smoothness × jerk matrix).\n- Streaming-loss extension (also needed eventually): feedbax `d67e303`.\n- Branch: `feature/loss-output-jerk` off `develop`.","files":null}]}